<title>NETHERLANDS: Wolters shares soften after H1 results.</title>
<headline>Wolters shares soften after H1 results.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Dutch publisher Wolters Kluwer NV retreated slightly in Amsterdam on Tuesday after the firm reported first-half net profits of 244 million guilders, in line with analysts' estimates.</p>
<p>The shares initially lost more ground, then recovered slightly after the group said it saw full-year fully-diluted EPS up around 19.5 percent to 8.40 guilders. The company had forecast annual growth of EPS of at least 15 percent.</p>
<p>At 0951 GMT, Wolters Kluwer shares stood down 2.00 guilders at 281.00.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
